// 49a — the arm shape B would have to emit, in a program someone would write.
//
// Under shape B the valve short-circuits on `Subject \ ParamType`: the members
// of the incoming value that are NOT in the stage's declared parameter type
// pass through untouched. That residual is a TYPE, and the emitter needs a
// runtime TEST for it.
//
// Here the subject is `binary` and the stage is declared over `string`. The
// residual is `binary \ string` — measured non-empty by the algebra, with no
// head F29 can spell and (measured with erlc) no BEAM guard behind it, because
// UTF-8 validity over a whole binary is not a guard expression.
//
// Nothing about this program is exotic: `string` is B#'s refinement of `binary`
// (F10), and declaring a stage over the narrower of the two is the ordinary
// reason to narrow at all.
module Narrow

public atom Run(binary raw)
Run(raw) -> Bytes(raw) |?> Decode()

private binary Bytes(binary raw)
Bytes(raw) -> raw

// The stage that narrows. Under shape B, `binary \ string` short-circuits here.
private atom Decode(string s)
Decode(s) -> :decoded
